lisa-design:
- platformAutomerge false (Renovate merges via API as ccf-release-bot) over GitHub native auto-merge: native auto-merge never applies the ccf-review ruleset bypass, so PRs sat REVIEW_REQUIRED forever. Accepted cost: merge lag up to one daily Renovate run.
- automergeStrategy "squash": the repos are squash-only; explicit rather than Renovate's "auto" detection.
- RENOVATE_LIVE mirrors CCF_BUMP_SYNC_LIVE / TRAIN_LIVE: schedule && var=='true' -> dry_run off, else inputs.dry_run || 'full'. Dispatch always follows its input.
- Scheduled manifest stays repos.mock.yaml (inputs.manifest || 'repos.mock.yaml'), as train.yml does; no manifest var introduced. Product rollout (W1-S4-T03) changes that fallback and sets RENOVATE_LIVE.
- Regression guard lives in the existing internal/renovate TestSharedPreset (platformAutomerge false, squash, non-major rule automergeType pr) rather than a new test.
- repo-settings' "allow auto-merge" is left untouched (PR #40 owns internal/reposettings); docs note Renovate no longer uses it.

lisa-selfreview:
pass 1 (strict): 1 finding.
- docs/renovate.md "Why Renovate merges": the merge-lag claim ("next daily run") relies on Renovate processing existing PRs outside the 8th/22nd schedule (updateNotScheduled defaults to true; automergeSchedule defaults to "at any time"). Not stated, so a reader could think merges wait for the next 8th/22nd. Fix: say so in the doc.
